 3. 👀 MAGA pushes Trump-tech divorce 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Photo: Nicholas Kamm/AFP via Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Prominent conservative thinkers and MAGA figures are seizing on Jensen Huang's affair with a suspected Chinese spy to pull President Trump away from his alliance with the tech right, Axios' Maria Curi writes. 

 These right-wing players view the midterm elections as proof that people across the political spectrum hate AI and data centers, and view Silicon Valley as too powerful. Oren Cass , founder of conservative think tank American Compass, said Trump's perception of China "has always been entirely commercial and transactional. His view was: 'We're getting screwed. I'm going to get a better deal.'"

 Cass, who has warned about Nvidia risks for more than a year, said the allegations of espionage are the strongest evidence yet that China isn't a commercial partner but an adversary that is going to "subvert the American political process in ways that end up humiliating the President." Keep reading . 

 
 
