 7. 🌊 California&#x27;s monster waves 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 People run as waves crash onto Beach Boulevard in Pacifica, Calif., near San Francisco on Saturday. Photo: Stephen Lam/San Francisco Chronicle via AP Huge waves — the biggest in nearly two years — pummeled the California coast over the weekend, inundating beaches and flooding local streets.

 Waves over 50 feet were recorded in San Mateo County, just south of San Francisco, on Saturday. Crowds gather to watch big waves and surfers at Mavericks Beach in Half Moon Bay, Calif., on Saturday. Photo: Tayfun Coskun/Anadolu via Getty Images In Southern California, iconic piers in Ventura, Manhattan Beach, Huntington Beach and San Diego's Pacific Beach were closed.

 The ongoing super El Niño — an unusually strong warming of Pacific waters — has raised coastal sea levels as warmer water expands and ocean currents shift, potentially allowing waves to push farther inland. Go deeper . 

 
 
