 8. 🦃 1 fun thing: The 100th parade 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 From left: Megan Moroney, Keke Palmer, Queen Latifah and Teddy Swims. Image: AP Megan Moroney, Teddy Swims, Queen Latifah, Keke Palmer, Jimmy Fallon &amp; The Roots and Smash Mouth will be part of the 100th Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade , stepping off in 10 days.

 The lineup includes a record-breaking 100 aerial balloons, including Bluey, Mickey Mouse and Hello Kitty . 📺 Fun fact: The 2½-mile parade has become such a tradition while we prep our turkeys that NBC's coverage ranks each year among the top 100 most-watched telecasts .

 The parade begins on NBC at 8:30 a.m. on Thanksgiving Day in all time zones and will feature a tribute to Dolly Parton led by actress and singer Megan Hilty, AP reports . The familiar hosts — Savannah Guthrie, Hoda Kotb and Al Roker from the "Today" show — will return on NBC and Peacock, with coverage running until noon. Full lineup ... 100 years of photos . 

 
 
